		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Bullet 2.23 released. improved penetration depth estimation]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=2337#p2337"><![CDATA[
Bullet 2.23 is available.<br><br>- Improved penetration depth estimation by sampling preferred directions. Currently penetrations involving boxes or triangles are improved: they report the triangle normal and box face normals.<br>- Some constraint solver experiments (randomizing the contact points)<br>- btMotionState is required now to synchronize world transform<br>- btCollisionObject is a class, member have accessors (sorry for the API changes)<br>- solid rendering of meshes (graphics)<br><br><a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediawiki-1.5.8/index.php?title=Download" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/mediaw ... e=Download</a><br><br>Thanks,<br>Erwin<br><a href="http://bulletphysics.com" class="postlink">http://bulletphysics.com</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Sat Nov 04, 2006 5:32 am</p><hr />
